[TEXT] ## Phase 2 — Branch: Real Symptoms Confirmed

Both probes return hard failures:
- **`web_server_1 → 10.1.1.2`**: `"Network is unreachable"` — no route exists on web_server_1 to reach outside its local segment.
- **`host_1_1_1_1 → 10.200.0.4`**: **Timeout** — packets go out but web_server_1 cannot reply (return path is broken).

The earlier "unknown" in the reachability map was **not** a DNS resolution failure — it was a genuine routing blackhole on `web_server_1`. The other web servers all reached hosts fine. This is a per-host routing fault.

**Active lead:** `web_server_1` has a missing or broken default gateway, preventing it from routing to any network outside 10.200.0.0/x. All three other web servers are healthy peers on the same segment, confirming this is isolated to one device.

